ArchiveEntry "Conjecture: Instability Beyond Routh-Hurwitz Boundary"

/*
 * STATUS: UNPROVED
 *
 * When |D2| > min(D1, K/D1), the linearized system has an eigenvalue
 * with positive real part. This should imply local instability:
 * trajectories starting arbitrarily close to the equilibrium can grow.
 *
 * In dL, instability is expressed using the diamond modality <{ODE}>:
 * there EXISTS a trajectory reaching a state far from the origin.
 *
 * The Routh-Hurwitz condition (from the characteristic polynomial
 * s^3 + (D1+D2)s^2 + (D1*D2+2K)s + K*(D1+D2)):
 *   D1+D2 > 0  AND  D1*D2+K > 0
 * When either fails, the system is linearly unstable.
 *
 * This conjecture formalizes: if D1*D2+K <= 0 (Routh condition 2 fails),
 * then there exist initial conditions near the origin whose trajectory
 * has H growing beyond any bound.
 *
 * Note: diamond proofs in KeYmaera X typically use dG (differential ghost)
 * to construct an explicit witness trajectory. This is non-trivial.
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real d1;
  Real d2;
  Real w1;
  Real w2;
  Real s;
  Real c;
End.

Problem
  \forall D1 \forall D2 \forall K (
    D1 > 0 & K > 0 & D2 < 0 & D1*D2 + K <= 0
    ->
    \forall eps (eps > 0 ->
      \exists d1 \exists d2 \exists w1 \exists w2 \exists s \exists c (
        s^2 + c^2 = 1 &
        w1^2 + w2^2 + 2*K*(1-c) < eps &
        <{d1' = w1,
          d2' = w2,
          w1' = -D1*w1 - K*s,
          w2' = -D2*w2 + K*s,
          s'  = c*(w1 - w2),
          c'  = -s*(w1 - w2)}>
        w1^2 + w2^2 + 2*K*(1-c) > 2*eps)))
End.

/* No Tactic — this is an open conjecture. */

End.
